# A loop of mandatory actions that raises a life total each time round is a draw, where one that lowers it ends in a loss
# (worldgorger-dragon-loop-with-rampaging-ferocidon-ends-when-its-controller-runs-out-of-life): CR 104.4b. Bot2 has
# Authority of the Consuls ("Creatures your opponents control enter tapped. Whenever a creature an opponent controls
# enters, you gain 1 life."). On turn 3 Bot1 animates its Entombed Worldgorger Dragon and the loop of the draw scenarios
# begins, every step of it forced; each time the Dragon enters - tapped - the Authority's ability, Bot2's alone, gains Bot2 1
# life. A life total going up never reaches what ends a game (CR 704.5a is 0 or less), and nothing here asks how much life
# anyone has: round after round the board is the same but for Bot2's life, no player can do anything but pass, and the loop
# has no way to stop. It goes round until the rules judge it endless, and the game is a draw. (Bot2's life total then is
# the engine's to say, not the rules': it is only more than 20.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Entomb
Animate Dead
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Worldgorger Dragon
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Authority of the Consuls
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Entomb.Cast
Bot1.Search(Worldgorger Dragon)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Authority of the Consuls.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot2.Battlefield = Plains; Authority of the Consuls
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Animate Dead.Cast(Bot1.Graveyard.Worldgorger Dragon)

[Expect]
Result = Draw
DrawReason = MandatoryLoop
Bot1.Status = (absent)
Bot2.Status = (absent)
Bot1.Life = 20
Turn = 3
Step = Main1
Stack.Count = 1
